Establish the actual, code-backed contract of the existing canonical-data/frontend-projection implementation before designing additional migrations. Trace runtime::UnlockedData<T>, its write-access notifier and move operations, frontend::Data/FrontEnd registration and lookup, TuiFrontEnd initialization/data_changed, and the ModelSelection and SessionStats implementations including their out-of-line translation units. Describe who owns each object, which thread may call each method, when locks are acquired and released relative to notifications, what stays at a stable address, and what happens during detached-state creation, session replacement and destruction. Locate definitions with findsymbol and follow callers; distinguish verified properties from intended properties that lack enforcement.

Explain dirty_.exchange(false) and races with concurrent publication, independent accumulated changed flags, initial refresh behavior, unknown values, full snapshot copying, cached string-reference lifetime and numeric RefreshResult values. Examine dependent projections, especially SessionStats consuming ModelSelection context-window metadata: identify single-consumer assumptions and whether multiple consumers could lose a notification. Determine which guarantees exist for coherent reads of multiple domains and which would need a new contract. Do not assume that atomic dirty flags alone provide object lifetime safety or cross-domain transactional coherence.

Produce a reference-contract artifact in this goal directory, registered in contents, with concrete file/symbol references, existing regression coverage, verified invariants, limitations and explicit verification questions. Include current backend-header exposure in frontend/TUI code and the smallest boundary changes needed by later goals. This is investigation and design only: do not modify production code or introduce a competing registry, generic state bag or notification architecture. Acceptance requires an accurate account of the existing pattern that the other audits can use, with unresolved assumptions clearly identified for reconciliation rather than presented as facts.
